Let $T\in\Lin(V,W)$, with $n=\dim V$, $p=\dim W$, and positive singular values $s_1,\ldots,s_r$. There are orthonormal bases $\mathcal E=(e_1,\ldots,e_n)$ of $V$ and $\mathcal F=(f_1,\ldots,f_p)$ of $W$ for which
\[
\Mat(T,\mathcal E,\mathcal F)_{j,k}
=
\begin{cases}
s_k,&j=k\le r,\\
0,&\text{otherwise}.
\end{cases}
\]
In particular, this matrix is diagonal, even when it is rectangular.
